  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building institutional capacity in Nomination of new Memory of the World (MoW) Registry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malawi is one of the few countries that nominates Memory of the World (MoW) registers due to lack of awareness and capacity to nominate. MoW is a UNESCO programme that promotes safeguarding and access of documentary heritage. The Registry is one of the means of achieving objectives of the MoW Programme thus preservation, accessibility and digitization of documentary heritage. This project aims to raise awareness of MoW and capacitate institutions in preparation of the Registry hence contributing towards implementation of the 2015 Recommendation concerning the Preservation of, and Access to, documentary heritage including in digital form.</narrative>
  </description>
